directly\n- **No meshes** directly\n- **Shader** is referenced implicitly only through the function name `apply_clip_and_fov_shader_to_view_model` on line 8\n- The function is a **stub** (`pass`), meaning the shader-application logic has not yet been implemented\n\nThis is essentially the file that needs to be implemented per the `task_config.json` instruction.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Full Contents of `weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader`\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/shaders/weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader`\n\n```glsl\n// NOTE: Shader automatically converted from Godot Engine 4.2.1.stable's StandardMaterial3D.\n\nshader_type spatial;\nrender_mode blend_mix,depth_draw_opaque,cull_disabled,diffuse_burley,specular_schlick_ggx;\nuniform vec4 albedo : source_color = vec4(1., 1., 1., 1.);\nuniform sampler2D texture_albedo : source_color,filter_linear_mipmap,repeat_enable;\nuniform float point_size : hint_range(0,128) = 1.0;\nuniform float roughness : hint_range(0,1) = 1.0;\nuniform sampler2D texture_metallic : hint_default_white,filter_linear_mipmap,repeat_enable;\nuniform vec4 metallic_texture_channel = vec4(0., 0., 0., 0.);\nuniform sampler2D texture_roughness : hint_roughness_g,filter_linear_mipmap,repeat_enable;\nuniform float specular = 0.5;\nuniform float metallic = 1.0;\nuniform sampler2D texture_normal : hint_roughness_normal,filter_linear_mipmap,repeat_enable;\nuniform float normal_scale : hint_range(-16,16) = 1.0;\nuniform vec3 uv1_scale = vec3(1., 1., 1.);\nuniform vec3 uv1_offset = vec3(0., 0., 0.);\nuniform vec3 uv2_scale = vec3(1., 1., 1.);\nuniform vec3 uv2_offset = vec3(0., 0., 0.);\n\nuniform float viewmodel_fov = 75.0f;\n\nvoid vertex() {\n\tUV = UV * uv1_scale.xy + uv1_offset.xy;\n\n\t/* VIEW MODEL Z CLIP FIX CODE */\n\tif (viewmodel_fov > 0.0) {\n\t\tfloat onetanfov = 1.0f / tan(0.5f * (viewmodel_fov * PI / 180.0f));\n\t\tfloat aspect = VIEWPORT_SIZE.x / VIEWPORT_SIZE.y;\n\t\t// Optional: Modify projection matrix to change the FOV\n\t\tPROJECTION_MATRIX[1][1] = -onetanfov;\n\t\tPROJECTION_MATRIX[0][0] = onetanfov / aspect;\n\t}\n\n\tPOSITION = PROJECTION_MATRIX * MODELVIEW_MATRIX * vec4(VERTEX.xyz, 1.0);\n\t// Mix vertex Z super close to clip plane, still maintaining some distance\n\t//POSITION.z = mix(POSITION.z, 0.0, 0.999); // Old version. Mix towards 0.0 (near z plane)\n\t// Above doesn't work for Godot 4.3 Z was reversed: https://godotengine.org/article/introducing-reverse-z/\n\t// Now we need to mix towards 1.0, but in clip space division by POSITION.w still hasn't happened.\n\t// So we mix z towards POSITION.w so that after perspective divsion, it will come out to 1.0 (near buffer since Z is reversed)\n\tPOSITION.z = mix(POSITION.z, POSITION.w, 0.9); // Could be higher mix val like 0.999 but I found 0.9 prevented 99% clipping w/ less artifacts than 0.999.\n\t/* END VIEW MODEL Z CLIP FIX CODE */\n}\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tvec2 base_uv = UV;\n\tvec4 albedo_tex = texture(texture_albedo, base_uv);\n\tALBEDO = albedo.rgb * albedo_tex.rgb;\n\tfloat metallic_tex = dot(texture(texture_metallic, base_uv), metallic_texture_channel);\n\tMETALLIC = metallic_tex * metallic;\n\tvec4 roughness_texture_channel = vec4(0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0);\n\tfloat roughness_tex = dot(texture(texture_roughness, base_uv), roughness_texture_channel);\n\tROUGHNESS = roughness_tex * roughness;\n\tSPECULAR = specular;\n\tNORMAL_MAP = texture(texture_normal, base_uv).rgb;\n\tNORMAL_MAP_DEPTH = normal_scale;\n}\n```\n\n**Key shader parameters relevant to the task:**\n- `uniform vec4 albedo : source_color` (default: white) -- the base color\n- `uniform float roughness : hint_range(0,1)` (default: 1.0)\n- `uniform float metallic` (default: 1.0)\n- `uniform float viewmodel_fov` (default: 75.0) -- the FOV parameter that controls the custom projection matrix and Z-clipping\n\n---\n\n## 6. All MeshInstance3D References\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`, line 21:\n```\n[node name=\"Knife\" type=\"MeshInstance3D\" parent=\"WeaponManager/ViewModel\"]\nmesh = SubResource(\"BoxMesh_1\")\n```\n- A `MeshInstance3D` node named **\"Knife\"** under `WeaponManager/ViewModel`\n- Uses `BoxMesh_1` (a `BoxMesh` with size `Vector3(0.2, 0.1, 0.5)`)\n- The mesh has a `StandardMaterial3D` (`StandardMaterial3D_1`) applied with:\n  - `albedo_color = Color(0.2, 0.7, 0.9, 1)` (a blue-ish color)\n  - `metallic = 0.2`\n  - `roughness = 0.8`\n- There is exactly **1 surface** on this mesh (BoxMesh has one surface by default)\n\n### `/workspace/task_config.json`, line 2:\n```\n\"Implement the view model clip shader swap on the weapon view model node. Add logic that finds MeshInstance3D nodes under the view model...\"\n```\n- The task instructions reference MeshInstance3D nodes generically (plural), indicating the implementation should be able to handle **any** MeshInstance3D found under the ViewModel node.\n\n### No GDScript code references MeshInstance3D:\n- The current `weapon_manager.gd` does **not** reference `MeshInstance3D` anywhere. The function `apply_clip_and_fov_shader_to_view_model` is a stub. This is the primary gap to be filled.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Findings\n\n| Aspect | Details |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Project** | Godot 4.4, GL Compatibility renderer, main scene `res://scenes/main.tscn` |\n| **View Model hierarchy** | `Main -> WeaponManager (with script) -> ViewModel -> Knife (MeshInstance3D)` |\n| **Weapon mesh** | BoxMesh (0.2 x 0.1 x 0.5), 1 surface with StandardMaterial3D (albedo=blue, metallic=0.2, roughness=0.8) |\n| **Shader file** | `/workspace/shaders/weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader` -- spatial shader with custom FOV projection + Z-clip fix, plus StandardMaterial3D-compatible uniforms (albedo, roughness, metallic, etc.) and a `viewmodel_fov` uniform |\n| **GDScript status** | `/workspace/scripts/weapon_manager.gd` has the function signature `apply_clip_and_fov_shader_to_view_model` defined but **not implemented** (it's a `pass` stub) |\n| **Task** | Implement the function to: find all MeshInstance3D under ViewModel, create a ShaderMaterial from the `.gdshader`, copy albedo/metallic/roughness from each surface's existing material, and set `viewmodel_fov` to 54.0 |\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f22a57c22ffenOU3PmLE8MK2H5","sessionId":"ses_f22a54989ffe60WjBOM4KU1Jj0","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790420104825,"end":1790420206928}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_02090dd5-9d22-47e5-bb29-9cabc31d1059"}},"id":"prt_0dd5ab66f0013e9iiS9N2mfi6K","sessionID":"ses_f22a57c22ffenOU3PmLE8MK2H5","messageID":"msg_0dd5a85cf001MkC4ghnWZ6LJ35"}}
